# daily-react-native-player — agent rules

## Naming ban (hard)

Never mention, cite, or compare to the commercial predecessor audio library by name in:
code, comments, tests, tickets, commit messages, README, ROADMAP, docs, or example app copy.

Speak only in product terms: speech queue, ambient channel, background playback, MediaSession, silence tracks, Daily Bible requirements.

Private study of gitignored `.reference/` trees is allowed for implementers. Do not paste that source into this repo. Do not link those paths from public docs.

## Product priorities

0. **Primary product — Daily Bible - Offline & Audio** ([Google Play](https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.coommark.dailybible), [App Store](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/daily-bible-offline-audio/id6754987448)). Bible-first acceptance beats speculative features until 0.1.0 is Bible-ready.
1. **P0 — Background playback** is non-negotiable: lock screen + notification remotes, now-playing metadata (title, artist, album, artwork, app identity), Android FGS `mediaPlayback`, iOS audio background mode, continue-after-kill policy.
2. **Bible-first** — implement the acceptance matrix in `docs/bible-acceptance.md` before speculative features.
3. **Ambient is consumer-opt-in** (lazy init; speech-only apps never create a second player) but **required for Bible-ready 0.1.0**.
4. **Silence tracks are core** — native-owned (Android SilenceMediaSource / iOS cached PCM WAV), first-class queue items.
5. **New Architecture only** — no old-architecture / legacy bridge support.

## Engineering rules

- Prefer minimalist diffs: smallest change that completes the ticket.
- Tests must pass before finishing a ticket (`yarn test`, `yarn lint`, `yarn typecheck` when applicable).
- Update docs after every ticket: `ROADMAP.md`, relevant `docs/*.md`, README feature status, `docs/api.md` for public API changes.
- Do not wrap a second independent focus-owning audio library for ambient. One native audio owner; ambient never requests focus.
- Prefer Expo Modules API + config plugin patterns. Install/use the `expo-module` skill when editing native code.
- Do not add TTS / ONNX / Sherpa into this package. Player consumes URLs / silence items only.
- Do not add MediaLibrary browsing, Android Auto, Cast, DASH/SmoothStreaming, or web player in v0.1.
- Example app must consume this package the way an npm consumer would (workspace / autolinking).

## Tickets

Work from `ROADMAP.md`. Do not skip P0 device verification for background controls when claiming those tickets done.
